                <pb facs="0214" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg120"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hall of
                            Sessions</hi>, <placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 22,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Miguel Urrutia, J. Pablo
                        Maldonado, Gregorio Enriquez, R. Aceña, Juan M. Rubio, Gustavo E.
                        Guzmán</hi>: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In discussing the report the following amendment was considered,
                            approved, and accepted by the committee:</p>
                        <p>“That the Executive be authorized, in case of necessity, to concede a
                            rebate up to 5 per cent. of the customs duties upon the cargo or
                            merchandise that the said steamers carry under the conditions of this
                            contract.”</p></quote></p>
            </div>
        </body>
